    findings: ["Homologous recombination gene mutation in 19%: germline 15%, somatic 4%; biallelic 11%, core 12%.", "First-line platinum progression-free survival hazard ratio 0.44 in the deficient group; no benefit from non-platinum.", "Core and biallelic mutations carry the higher genomic instability and the larger benefit."],
